    <item>
      <title>## SHOW NOTES

** The $75 Billion AI Holiday Shopping Spree: SoftBank’s Scramble, Waymo Mayhem, and The Inescapable Prompt Injection**

**</title>
      <description>** Just days before the holiday break, the AI industry is hemorrhaging cash, racking up debt, and facing existential security threats. We unpack SoftBank’s desperate $22.5 billion funding scramble and ByteDance’s equally staggering $23 billion commitment, revealing a market driven by fear, not innovation. Plus, we dive into the catastrophic failure of Waymo vehicles creating traffic purgatory during a city power outage, and get Rufus’s legal perspective on who exactly is liable when the agents go rogue.

***</description>
